  message: "Drill-down **changed the diagnosis significantly**. The 9 specific externals in the original filing are driven by a different bug than the title suggests. Both bugs are real, but they're independent.\n\n## Bug E1 (what the title describes)\n\n`_detect_src_layout(repo_root)` at py.py:1471 only detects a single top-level `repo/src/`. For monorepos where each package has its own `packages/<pkg>/src/<mod>/` layout (hypergumbo, many Python monorepos using hatch/PDM), this returns `None`. The analyzer then uses `rel_path.relative_to(repo_root)` in `_module_name_from_path` (py.py:1520), producing module identifiers like `packages.hypergumbo-core.src.hypergumbo_core.taxonomy` — path-shaped, with invalid Python syntax (hyphens).\n\n**This bug is real but self-consistent.** Every hypergumbo Python file's `importing_module` comes out in the same buggy form. The global_symbols table keys match the buggy module names. Internal cross-file resolution still WORKS for functions and classes because both sides use the same (buggy) qualifier. External-facing surfaces (sketch output, slice module names, IR serialization) just get ugly identifiers.\n\n## Bug E2 (what actually caused the 9 externals)\n\n**Module-level `NAME = ...` assignments are not indexed as Symbols in the Python analyzer.** Verified by listing all taxonomy.py Symbol kinds on hypergumbo's self-analysis: `method=53, class=12, function=8, module=1`. Zero constants. Yet taxonomy.py clearly defines `LANGUAGE_ALIASES`, `LANGUAGE_EXTENSIONS`, `SOURCE_EXTENSIONS` at module scope.\n\npy.py has a `_collect_module_constants` helper at line 842, but it's used only for internal URL-path resolution in route decorators (py.py:2118) — it never emits `Symbol` objects into the `symbols` list that becomes global_symbols.\n\nWhen `from .taxonomy import LANGUAGE_ALIASES` runs:\n1. Relative import resolves to `(module=taxonomy, name=LANGUAGE_ALIASES)`.\n2. `_lookup_symbol_by_module(global_symbols, \"taxonomy\", \"LANGUAGE_ALIASES\")` — MISS (constant not indexed).\n3. Fall through to external — `create_boundary_nodes` synthesises a tier-3 node.\n\n## Scope\n\n| Bug | Manifestation | Count on hypergumbo |\n|---|---|---|\n| E1 (monorepo src/ layout) | Module qualifiers have `packages.<pkg-with-dashes>.src.<mod>.` shape; sketch / slice output ugly; tier-1 file paths in IR show as hyphen-dot hybrids | Affects 100% of importing-module derivations in the repo |\n| E2 (module-level constants not indexed) | Unresolved imports of any `UPPERCASE_CONSTANT` or other module-scope Assign; externalises as tier-3 | **151 ALL-CAPS constant-shaped externals** on self-analysis: PASS_VERSION, SCHEMA_VERSION, DEFAULT_EXCLUDES, EXIT_SUCCESS, EXIT_USER_ERROR, CHARS_PER_TOKEN, EXCLUDED_KINDS, LANGUAGE_ALIASES, LANGUAGE_EXTENSIONS, SOURCE_EXTENSIONS, … |\n\nOn hypergumbo the 9 externals I originally flagged are a subset of the 151 ALL-CAPS externals. The duplicated `PASS_VERSION` / `DEFAULT_EXCLUDES` entries (one `python:hypergumbo_core.X:0-0:NAME:symbol`, one `python:packages.hypergumbo-core.src.hypergumbo_core.X:0-0:NAME:symbol`) reveal both bugs interacting — some callers write absolute imports (`from hypergumbo_core.ir import PASS_VERSION`), others relative (`from .ir import PASS_VERSION`). Each produces a different synthetic external because E2 fails for both AND E1 makes the relative-import path derive a different qualifier than the absolute one.\n\n## Fix directions\n\n**E1** — extend `_detect_src_layout` to return a *list* of source roots and scan for any directory structure matching `**/src/<importable>/` where `<importable>` is a dir with `__init__.py`. Update `_module_name_from_path` to try each source_root and use whichever the file is under. On a typical non-monorepo this collapses to the current single-root behaviour. Test fixture: a synthetic `packages/pkg-a/src/pkg_a/` + `packages/pkg-b/src/pkg_b/` layout.\n\n**E2** — extend the Python analyzer's symbol-extraction pass to emit `Symbol(kind=\"constant\", …)` for module-level `ast.Assign` and `ast.AnnAssign` nodes whose target is a `Name`. Reuse the `_collect_module_constants` walk logic. Register the new kind in the IR `Symbol.kind` allowlist (if one exists). Update `_lookup_symbol_by_module` to look up constants.\n\n## Should this be one item or two?\n\nThe bugs are independent and fix directions don't overlap (E1 is in layout detection, E2 is in symbol extraction). My instinct is to **split**: keep this item (WI-davan) scoped to E1 and file a new item for E2 at equal priority. E2 is arguably the higher-impact bug (151 externals vs. mostly-cosmetic identifier ugliness from E1), so I'd file E2 as todo_hard P2 as well.\n\nDeferring that split decision to the human — if you'd rather keep them combined, the original description stands (with this note correcting the root-cause attribution). Either way, the self-analysis reproduction for E2 is straightforward: count ALL-CAPS external_symbol nodes under `python:` in a run that indexes constants, expect → 0.\n\n## Validation\n\nBoth bugs are validatable on hypergumbo itself. For E1: after fix, module qualifiers should not contain the path-shaped `.src.` or hyphenated segments. For E2: ALL-CAPS constant-shaped externals should drop from 151 → near-zero. Tag `awaits_bakeoff_validation` with a claim for each."  # bd00
